{{also|ohi-|ʻohi|OHI}}

==Estonian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|et|urj-fin-pro|*ohja}}, cognate to {{cog|fi|ohja}} and {{cog|vot|õhjõ}}. Possibly a loan from {{der|et|gem-pro|*ansijō}}.

===Noun===
{{et-noun|ohja|ohja}}

# [[rein]]

====Declension====
{{et-decl-tühi|oh|||ja|i}}

==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|fi|past}}
Lative: {{affix|fi|ohi|pos1=noun|id1=side|-i|id2=adverbial}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fi-p|(*)}}

====Adverb====
{{fi-adv}}

# {{lb|fi|spatial}} [[past]], [[beyond]]
#: {{ux|fi|Minun piti kääntyä toisesta risteyksestä oikealle, mutta ajoinkin '''ohi'''.|I was supposed to turn right from the second intersection but I missed it.|lit=drove '''past'''}}
# {{lb|fi|temporal}} [[over]] {{gloss|discontinued; ended or concluded}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Se on '''ohi''' nyt.|It is '''over''' now.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''ohi''' on|[it] is '''over''' [now] (e.g. referring to military service)}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The inflected forms shown in the table are used as adverbs, postpositions and prepositions, see appropriate entries.

=====Inflection=====
{{fi-decl-pron/ohi-}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fi|ohitse}}

====Postposition====
{{fi-postp}} {{+obj|fi|gen}}

# {{lb|fi|spatial}} [[by]], [[past]] {{gloss|when one goes ''through'' the space that is ''next to'' something}}
#: {{ux|fi|Pallo pyöri tuolin '''ohi''' ja ovesta ulos.|The ball rolled ''by'' the chair and out of the door.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Pallo pyöri minun '''ohitseni'''.|The ball rolled '''past''' me.}}
# {{lb|fi|spatial}} [[wide]]
#: {{ux|fi|Nuoli meni maalin '''ohi'''.|The arrow fell '''wide''' of the mark.}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|fi||ohi}} cannot take a possessive suffix; {{m|fi|ohitse}} is used instead if possessive forms are desired.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fi|ohitse}}

====Preposition====
{{head|fi|preposition}} {{+obj|fi|ela}}

# {{lb|fi|spatial}} [[past]] {{gloss|when going or having gone past, i.e. passing, usually physically}}
#: {{ux|fi|Olimme jo '''ohi''' sillasta, kun onnettomuus tapahtui.|We were already '''past''' the bridge, when the accident took place.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fi|ohitse}}

====Interjection====
{{head|fi|intj}}

# [[miss]]! {{gloss|used like an interjection to indicate that a shot missed the target}}

